  "tagline": "GPU-native columnar SQL database with visual analytics, fully open-sourced by NVIDIA in 2026.",
  "description": "HeavyDB (formerly MapD and OmniSciDB) is an in-memory columnar SQL engine that compiles queries with LLVM and runs them across GPUs, making interactive scans and geospatial joins over billions of rows feasible on a single server. NVIDIA acquired HEAVY.AI in 2025, and in October 2026 released v10.0 with the whole platform open source under Apache 2.0, including the Immerse dashboard UI, the GPU rendering engine, HeavyConnect foreign tables and HeavyRF. It is a strong option for geospatial and telemetry visualization on NVIDIA hardware; it needs GPUs and the community is still forming around the new release.",
